WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.960
[Hank Green]: Good morning, John!

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:02.540
[Casey Neisat]: What really blew me away

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:04.160
is the sense of community,

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:05.300
the sense of excitement;

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.080
all of this energy that's surrounding

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:08.300
this event!

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:08.800
[Alli Speed]: Seeing

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.200
how YouTube changes.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.080
[Connor Franta]: The first VidCon I ever went to,

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.040
I was a viewer;

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:14.320
so, I watched things like this,

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.340
but I w- and I was right in there.

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:18.240
[Felicia Day]: Video, to me, is a way to make people feel like they belong.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:19.200
[Kevin Alloca]: You are, basically,

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.300
the early pioneers of the new and different medium.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.120
[Franchesca Ramsey]: I wasn't seeing

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:24.000
people like me represented

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:25.020
in television.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:26.920
[Katie Couric]: This is my first, uh, VidCon;

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:27.480
and I..

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:28.380
feel

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:29.420
very old.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:01:44.540
["Come Out To Play" by Pomplamoose plays]

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:46.420
[Hank Green]: VidCon 2016,

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:47.140
the 7th

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:47.640
Annual

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:48.500
VidCon,

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:49.500
is gonna be a thing.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:52.160
June 23rd to the 25th, in Anaheim;

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:54.320
and registration is available now!..

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:56.600
Because VidCon 2015 went pretty well,

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:59.540
we're basically going to be doing the same thing that we did last year,

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:00.620
just with a little more!

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:01.660
We'll have more stages,

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:02.680
we'll have more space,

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:04.060
we'll have more special guests...

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:06.300
Our goal with VidCon has always been to reflect the

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:07.900
state of online video.

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:09.660
And thus, as online video has grown,

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:10.740
so has VidCon.

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:11.240
But(!),

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:13.540
one thing that we haven't been particularly good in reflecting,

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:14.340
I feel like,

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:16.600
is the explosion in gaming content;

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:17.940
and I feel bad about that!!

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:18.460
Because streamers,

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:19.380
and YouTube gamers,

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:20.120
are huge!!

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:21.180
It's a huge thing,

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:22.760
and I feel like we just haven't been good

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:24.540
at- at inviting that in

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:26.060
and making it a priority at VidCon;

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:27.360
so, I really want to do that this year.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:29.920
In order to make sure that I do, like, at least an okay job of that;

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:32.920
I have just been trying to understand the YouTube gaming world.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:34.300
And the Twitch world, as well..

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:35.100
It so

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:35.600
diverse!!

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:36.600
It's so huge!

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:37.660
If a few people watching

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:39.520
want to suggest any gamers to me,

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:42.400
or any interesting things in the gaming world that I should check out,

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:43.040
please do that

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:43.860
in the comments!

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:44.500
I'll be looking.

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:46.100
Most things that will be pretty much the same:

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:47.080
we have the same tracks;

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:48.020
the Creator Track,

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:48.780
the Community Track,

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:49.800
and the Industry Track;

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:50.640
and the signings and photos

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:52.040
will be taken in the same way that they were last year,

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:52.600
with a lottery,

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:54.240
where you rank your favourite creators,

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.380
and then, based on your preferences

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:56.180
and availability,

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:57.040
you get some signings.

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:59.260
And that way, you don't have to wait in line for hours and hours!

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:00.060
And, I know that some people

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:02.340
do want to wait in line for hours and hours,

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:02.840
but..

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:04.680
first-come, first-serve is how we did it in 2014,

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:05.180
and that..

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:05.980
turned out..

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:06.700
[Laughing] kinda bad!

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:07.200
Other,

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.880
completely unrelated to VidCon, news:

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:09.660
the Project For Awesome

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:11.220
is gonna be on December 11th and 12th;

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:12.640
so, if you want to make a Project For Awesome video,

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:13.780
you've gotta start thinking about it.

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:15.740
If you don't know what the Project For Awesome is;

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:18.220
we will be talking more about it

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:18.920
during

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:19.820
Pizzamas!

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:20.780
If you don't know what

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:21.280
Pizzamas

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:21.900
is;

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:22.460
I'm about to tell you.

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:23.840
We celebrate Pizzamas

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:25.200
here on the VlogBrothers channel;

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:25.860
and last year,

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:26.740
we celebrated that

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:27.500
with two weeks

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:29.520
of Brotherhood 2.0-style videos,

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:30.060
which means

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:32.460
a video every weekday from one of us,

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:33.120
Hank or John.

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:33.700
Starting Monday,

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:35.240
there will be a video every weekday

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:36.080
for two weeks(!),

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:37.220
and it will be great!!

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:37.760
In addition to that,

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:38.360
we do a bunch

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:39.380
of Limited Edition

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:40.520
Pizza John shirts.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:41.020
This is one from

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:41.680
last year!

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:43.100
You will not be able to get it this year;

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.320
but, you will be able to get a number of very cool ones

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:46.500
that I will not show you

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:47.640
until Pizzamas begins.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:48.220
Which, it will,

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:48.920
on Monday,

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:49.520
with my video!

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:50.580
And then, John,

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:52.580
I will see you on Tuesday.

